I'll make some escargot.

1139
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:16,920
Scrambled eggs with tomatoes?

1140
00:39:17,640 --> 00:39:18,200
Okay.

1141
00:39:18,200 --> 00:39:19,040
Of course.

1142
00:39:20,280 --> 00:39:21,000
There are cucumbers.

1143
00:39:21,000 --> 00:39:22,280
Then let's make Moo Shu Pork, okay?

1144
00:39:23,968 --> 00:39:24,760
(Who are you asking?)

1145
00:39:24,760 --> 00:39:25,880
You guys...

1146
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:26,680
Your group.

1147
00:39:26,760 --> 00:39:27,640
You are your own group.

1148
00:39:27,776 --> 00:39:28,992
(A clear boundary)

1149
00:39:29,696 --> 00:39:30,600
(Heartbreaking for Nai)

1150
00:39:30,600 --> 00:39:31,440
Don't discuss it.

1151
00:39:31,440 --> 00:39:32,680
Don't consult Yuning for everything.

1152
00:39:35,640 --> 00:39:37,880
(Don't underestimate me)
I won't look for him at all later.

1153
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:39,520
(I'm also good)
You guys don't look for us either.

1154
00:39:46,680 --> 00:39:47,680
(Song Qian returns)
Qian.

1155
00:39:47,680 --> 00:39:48,760
Qian.

1156
00:39:49,400 --> 00:39:50,160
I'm here.

1157
00:39:50,320 --> 00:39:50,960
Are you okay?

1158
00:39:51,640 --> 00:39:52,120
How are you doing?

1159
00:39:53,240 --> 00:39:54,400
- Much better than this morning.
- Her throat is already gone.

1160
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:56,000
Did you take medicine?

1161
00:39:56,640 --> 00:39:57,760
How does your throat feel now?

1162
00:39:58,640 --> 00:39:59,720
It's a bit sore now.

1163
00:39:59,720 --> 00:40:01,080
But I can talk normally.

1164
00:40:01,840 --> 00:40:03,040
Just talk less.

1165
00:40:03,600 --> 00:40:04,640
Come on, Lin Yi. Let me interview you.

1166
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:05,408
(Eggplant attack)

1167
00:40:07,520 --> 00:40:08,760
Why did you just shove it into my mouth?

1168
00:40:10,760 --> 00:40:12,000
Come on, everyone.

1169
00:40:12,440 --> 00:40:14,600
Welcome to the final of Wow The World S2

1170
00:40:14,600 --> 00:40:18,880
Chinese-French fusion dishes
cooking competition.

1171
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:20,224
(The final?)

1172
00:40:20,320 --> 00:40:20,960
Alright.

1173
00:40:21,840 --> 00:40:23,080
(What a direct pass)
They haven't even filmed the auditions.

1174
00:40:23,080 --> 00:40:24,280
Where's the preliminary round?

1175
00:40:25,200 --> 00:40:26,400
Film it back in China.

1176
00:40:27,040 --> 00:40:28,000
As you can see,

1177
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:29,520
we've prepared a variety

1178
00:40:29,520 --> 00:40:31,480
of Chinese and French ingredients.

1179
00:40:31,480 --> 00:40:33,000
The two teams need to each complete

1180
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:34,840
two fusion dishes within 60 minutes.

1181
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,600
One fuses French ingredients

1182
00:40:36,600 --> 00:40:38,560
with Chinese culinary techniques,

1183
00:40:38,880 --> 00:40:40,480
while the other captures
the very essence of French cuisine

1184
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:41,960
using Chinese ingredients.

1185
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:43,560
After cooking is finished,

1186
00:40:43,560 --> 00:40:45,400
two professional chefs

1187
00:40:45,400 --> 00:40:47,360
will comment on your dishes

1188
00:40:47,360 --> 00:40:48,840
and select the winning team.

1189
00:40:48,840 --> 00:40:50,200
The winning team will receive

1190
00:40:50,200 --> 00:40:52,200
the honorary title
of "Earth Cooking King."

1191
00:40:54,112 --> 00:40:56,960
(Determined to win)

1192
00:40:57,080 --> 00:40:59,320
First, let's welcome the two judges.

1193
00:41:01,120 --> 00:41:03,160
- Hello, Masters.
- Hello, Masters.

1194
00:41:03,456 --> 00:41:04,480
(Jean-François Rouquette, Executive Chef
of a Michelin one-star restaurant)

1195
00:41:04,480 --> 00:41:04,960
(Zhang Huan)
Hello.

1196
00:41:04,960 --> 00:41:05,536
(Executive Chef
of a Michelin-recommended restaurant)

1197
00:41:06,120 --> 00:41:08,520
I thought they were helpers.

1198
00:41:08,520 --> 00:41:10,120
So they are judges, right?

1199
00:41:10,120 --> 00:41:11,840
They're here to taste.

1200
00:41:11,840 --> 00:41:13,240
The chefs are helping us out?

1201
00:41:13,240 --> 00:41:13,880
Aren't we...

1202
00:41:14,592 --> 00:41:15,800
(Wishful thinking)

1203
00:41:15,800 --> 00:41:16,600
To help you

1204
00:41:16,600 --> 00:41:19,040
gain a better understanding
of Chinese and French cuisine

1205
00:41:19,040 --> 00:41:20,200
and get into the zone faster,

1206
00:41:20,200 --> 00:41:21,720
we've also asked the two chefs

1207
00:41:21,720 --> 00:41:22,600
to briefly share

1208
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:24,400
their views
on Chinese-French fusion cuisine.

1209
00:41:24,672 --> 00:41:26,624
(Waiting for the masters
to highlight the key points)

1210
00:41:26,720 --> 00:41:28,720
The soul of French cuisine

1211
00:41:28,720 --> 00:41:30,560
lies in it being

1212
00:41:30,560 --> 00:41:33,240
an art of fusion.

1213
00:41:33,240 --> 00:41:35,320
It fuses plating,

1214
00:41:35,320 --> 00:41:36,640
texture,

1215
00:41:36,640 --> 00:41:37,520
flavor,

1216
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:39,520
and aesthetics.

1217
00:41:40,000 --> 00:41:40,960
Overall,

1218
00:41:40,960 --> 00:41:42,440
it's a holistic experience,

1219
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:44,000
an awakening of the five senses.

1220
00:41:45,120 --> 00:41:46,080
Aesthetic competition.

1221
00:41:46,760 --> 00:41:47,560
The City of Art.

1222
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:48,760
Art, truly art.

1223
00:41:49,360 --> 00:41:51,640
Regarding how to make
Chinese-French fusion dishes,

1224
00:41:51,640 --> 00:41:53,280
I think you first need to understand

1225
00:41:53,280 --> 00:41:55,480
the cooking structure
of Chinese-French fusion cuisine.

1226
00:41:55,480 --> 00:41:58,240
French cuisine
emphasizes subtraction and precision.

1227
00:41:59,040 --> 00:41:59,560
Heat control,

1228
00:41:59,560 --> 00:42:00,080
temperature,

1229
00:42:00,080 --> 00:42:01,800
and time all need to be very precise.

1230
00:42:02,000 --> 00:42:04,360
It relies on the sauce
to unify the flavor of the entire dish.

1231
00:42:04,640 --> 00:42:06,200
Chinese cuisine is the exact opposite.

1232
00:42:06,360 --> 00:42:07,960
It emphasizes addition

1233
00:42:08,160 --> 00:42:09,880
and a sense of proportion
with heat control.

1234
00:42:10,360 --> 00:42:12,960
Stir-frying uses an instant high heat
to lock in freshness,

1235
00:42:13,120 --> 00:42:15,200
along with layers of various seasonings

1236
00:42:15,200 --> 00:42:16,280
to create a complex flavor profile.

1237
00:42:16,600 --> 00:42:18,080
It doesn't rely on precise calculation,

1238
00:42:18,080 --> 00:42:19,520
but on the chef's touch.

1239
00:42:19,520 --> 00:42:21,000
But a chef's feeling
honed over many years.

1240
00:42:21,320 --> 00:42:24,080
So the essence
of Chinese-French fusion cuisine

1241
00:42:24,080 --> 00:42:26,160
lies in combining
French cooking techniques

1242
00:42:26,160 --> 00:42:28,240
with the soul of Chinese cuisine,

1243
00:42:28,560 --> 00:42:30,000
which is what we call
the flavor profile.

1244
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:33,000
This way, it allows guests
to experience different tastes

1245
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:34,840
through the same ingredients.

1246
00:42:35,280 --> 00:42:36,600
(Song Qian)
It can also let guests feel

1247
00:42:36,600 --> 00:42:37,840
a distinct cultural

1248
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:39,920
exchange and collision between the two.

1249
00:42:40,672 --> 00:42:41,408
(Knowledge has entered the brain)

1250
00:42:41,880 --> 00:42:42,760
Important information.

1251
00:42:43,040 --> 00:42:45,360
Okay, through the guidance
of the two chefs,

1252
00:42:45,360 --> 00:42:47,240
you all should have some ideas

1253
00:42:47,240 --> 00:42:48,560
for this fusion cuisine showdown.

1254
00:42:48,880 --> 00:42:49,400
Next,

1255
00:42:49,680 --> 00:42:51,840
please each designate
one French cuisine ingredient

1256
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:52,760
for the other side

1257
00:42:53,080 --> 00:42:56,000
as a mandatory ingredient
for the Chinese-style French cuisine.

1258
00:42:56,480 --> 00:42:57,840
(Fei has something to say)
I think actually,

1259
00:42:57,840 --> 00:43:00,160
many creative ideas come

1260
00:43:00,400 --> 00:43:00,920
from pressure.

1261
00:43:00,920 --> 00:43:03,000
That kind of wildflower

1262
00:43:03,000 --> 00:43:05,080
growing in the cracks
is the most beautiful.

1263
00:43:05,632 --> 00:43:08,480
(What does it mean?)

1264
00:43:08,600 --> 00:43:10,240
So we will give you a challenge.

1265
00:43:10,240 --> 00:43:11,480
You don't need to give us a challenge.

1266
00:43:11,480 --> 00:43:11,960
Okay?

1267
00:43:11,960 --> 00:43:12,384
(Scheme's all over his face)

1268
00:43:14,120 --> 00:43:16,280
Why are we the only ones in the cracks?

1269
00:43:16,280 --> 00:43:18,200
Because he wants us
to survive in the cracks.

1270
00:43:18,200 --> 00:43:20,240
Then why are we the only ones
in the cracks?

1271
00:43:20,240 --> 00:43:21,248
(Not succumbing to pressure)

1272
00:43:23,200 --> 00:43:24,120
Let's do it this way.

1273
00:43:24,120 --> 00:43:26,720
We'll each choose for the other side.

1274
00:43:26,720 --> 00:43:27,880
For example, this is a vegetable
I haven't seen before,

1275
00:43:27,880 --> 00:43:29,160
