1314
00:44:44,160 --> 00:44:45,184
(The showdown officially begins)

1315
00:44:45,480 --> 00:44:46,120
Come on.

1316
00:44:46,120 --> 00:44:47,520
Let's figure out what to cook.

1317
00:44:47,520 --> 00:44:49,280
Let's find a spot. Don't let them hear.

1318
00:44:49,560 --> 00:44:50,528
(Extremely guarded)
Alright, let's research.

1319
00:44:50,528 --> 00:44:52,240
Right here at our stove.

1320
00:44:52,240 --> 00:44:53,200
Seems like we really want to win.

1321
00:44:53,472 --> 00:44:54,760
(It's heating up)

1322
00:44:54,760 --> 00:44:55,680
Actually, this thing is simple.

1323
00:44:56,360 --> 00:44:57,120
Simple in what way?

1324
00:44:57,360 --> 00:44:58,880
I think this is a good thing.

1325
00:44:58,880 --> 00:44:59,880
And what's the reason?

1326
00:44:59,880 --> 00:45:01,800
The bitterness is actually in the juice.

1327
00:45:02,160 --> 00:45:04,280
We can blanch it in water a little

1328
00:45:04,280 --> 00:45:06,160
(Passing by and overhearing)
and turn it into a container.

1329
00:45:06,160 --> 00:45:06,640
You know?

1330
00:45:07,240 --> 00:45:09,000
(Great idea)
It's a thing to hold the food.

1331
00:45:09,400 --> 00:45:09,920
(Likes it)
So cool.

1332
00:45:09,920 --> 00:45:10,520
This is so cool.

1333
00:45:11,040 --> 00:45:12,840
(Liu Yuning, true kitchen legend)
We'll stuff the filling into this.

1334
00:45:12,840 --> 00:45:13,560
(Liu Yuning, a triple-threat and a catch)
It...

1335
00:45:13,840 --> 00:45:14,720
It's made us the winner.

1336
00:45:14,720 --> 00:45:14,920
It's called

1337
00:45:14,920 --> 00:45:15,680
A Lone Boat.

1338
00:45:15,680 --> 00:45:16,200
Right?

1339
00:45:16,200 --> 00:45:17,800
(Wow)
A Lone Boat.

1340
00:45:20,560 --> 00:45:21,160
That's the idea.

1341
00:45:21,160 --> 00:45:22,320
We've already won.

1342
00:45:22,622 --> 00:45:24,240
(Can't be low-key at all)

1343
00:45:24,240 --> 00:45:25,080
Stop talking.

1344
00:45:25,080 --> 00:45:25,520
Stop...

1345
00:45:25,520 --> 00:45:27,080
Stop talking.

1346
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:30,000
Naiwen, we've already won. Goodbye.

1347
00:45:30,480 --> 00:45:31,200
How is that possible?

1348
00:45:32,400 --> 00:45:33,840
(Gradually approaching)
It means that we'll be using it, right?

1349
00:45:33,840 --> 00:45:34,680
Then you guys...

1350
00:45:34,680 --> 00:45:35,840
(Activating defense mode)
Don't say it. Don't let him see.

1351
00:45:35,840 --> 00:45:36,160
Okay.

1352
00:45:36,416 --> 00:45:37,880
(Volume)

1353
00:45:37,880 --> 00:45:39,720
No need to discuss so quietly.

1354
00:45:40,240 --> 00:45:41,280
(BA Honglei)
Please move aside.

1355
00:45:41,840 --> 00:45:42,720
Please move aside.

1356
00:45:42,720 --> 00:45:43,600
Let's bask in the sun.

1357
00:45:43,600 --> 00:45:44,256
(Containing him)

1358
00:45:44,256 --> 00:45:44,976
Come here to sunbathe.

1359
00:45:45,120 --> 00:45:46,528
Let's, the old couple, bask in the sun.

1360
00:45:46,528 --> 00:45:47,840
The sun is quite comfortable.

1361
00:45:47,840 --> 00:45:49,240
(Each one scheming harder
than the other)

1362
00:45:49,240 --> 00:45:51,000
How about this?
You two think of one together.

1363
00:45:51,000 --> 00:45:51,680
You make one.

1364
00:45:51,680 --> 00:45:52,760
Don't let me do it all.

1365
00:45:52,760 --> 00:45:54,440
I'll help you sort out the whole logic.

1366
00:45:54,440 --> 00:45:55,320
You execute it.

1367
00:45:55,392 --> 00:45:57,536
(Strongest head chef
and strongest sous chef)

1368
00:45:57,760 --> 00:45:59,320
I feel like we have to make one

1369
00:45:59,320 --> 00:46:00,760
with their most familiar ingredient,

1370
00:46:00,760 --> 00:46:03,680
but create a flavor they least expect.

1371
00:46:03,680 --> 00:46:04,000
Yes.

1372
00:46:04,760 --> 00:46:05,560
Let me see the chicken.

1373
00:46:06,600 --> 00:46:07,680
The chicken is okay.

1374
00:46:08,160 --> 00:46:09,120
Salt and Scallion Chicken Thighs?

1375
00:46:09,120 --> 00:46:09,600
Okay.

1376
00:46:09,952 --> 00:46:11,000
(Dishes: 1. Salt and Scallion
Chicken Thighs with Chicory)

1377
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,600
I'll teach you a dish.

1378
00:46:12,600 --> 00:46:13,880
It's fried meat.

1379
00:46:15,440 --> 00:46:16,080
Soft-fried Pork.

1380
00:46:16,080 --> 00:46:16,960
I'll mix the batter for you.

1381
00:46:16,960 --> 00:46:18,000
You guys do the frying, okay?

1382
00:46:18,000 --> 00:46:19,320
(2. Soft-fried Pork)
Fried meat is Chinese cuisine?

1383
00:46:19,600 --> 00:46:20,400
Of course.

1384
00:46:20,400 --> 00:46:21,360
But we use

1385
00:46:21,360 --> 00:46:23,640
the Western seasoning and plating.

1386
00:46:23,640 --> 00:46:24,440
For the plating,

1387
00:46:24,440 --> 00:46:25,160
I'll do some carving for you.

1388
00:46:25,760 --> 00:46:28,080
Carved flowers plus this,
we've already won.

1389
00:46:28,512 --> 00:46:29,088
(Nailed it)

1390
00:46:29,480 --> 00:46:30,040
We've won.

1391
00:46:30,760 --> 00:46:32,080
Let's just award the prize now.

1392
00:46:32,608 --> 00:46:34,120
(Arrogant)

1393
00:46:34,120 --> 00:46:34,960
Hurry up and eat.

1394
00:46:37,520 --> 00:46:38,200
(Pressure)
Let's start now.

1395
00:46:38,200 --> 00:46:39,640
Otherwise, it'll take too long.

1396
00:46:39,640 --> 00:46:40,400
Let's handle this first.

1397
00:46:40,400 --> 00:46:41,480
Let's handle this first.

1398
00:46:41,800 --> 00:46:42,880
To do the Chinese-style French cuisine,

1399
00:46:42,880 --> 00:46:44,040
